# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files — NEVER commit a real one. `.env.example` is the exception and is
# tracked on purpose: it documents which keys a deploy needs (WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY
# etc.) without carrying a single value.
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Strategy briefs live in chats, NEVER in the repo (brief v5's own rule) � they carry internal pricing.
debugswift-master-brief-v*.md

# Playwright / MCP browser artifacts (console logs, page snapshots, reports)
/.playwright-mcp/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/

# Editor & OS cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*~

# Loose images / video / scratch dropped at the repo ROOT (design references,
# AI exports, screenshots). Real site assets live under /public and are NOT
# matched by these root-only globs.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
/*.gif
/*.mp4
/*.pdf

# Local Claude Code tooling (hooks, agent definitions, skill copy). Machine
# setup rather than repo content — ignored, same as the other two repos.
/.claude/

# DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE FROM THE MARKETING AND BLOG REPOS, 28 Jul 2026.
#
# Both of those gitignore /docs/ and /CLAUDE.md. This repo TRACKS them, and the
# reason is a lesson those repos already paid for: the marketing repo's Round 10
# doc-sync pass found that because docs/ is gitignored, "every doc edit is
# local-only, untracked, no history, no rollback, no diff to review" — recorded
# at the time as the real backfire risk.
#
# In this repo docs/copy/tools.md is not background material, it is the source
# the components are built from, it is an unapproved draft the owner is expected
# to edit, and losing its history would mean losing the record of what he
# changed. CLAUDE.md is the repo's operating rules and a fresh clone needs them.
#
# Neither file carries pricing or anything else the marketing brief's
# "never in the repo" rule was written to protect.
#
# If the owner would rather keep the convention uniform across all three repos,
# add /docs/ and /CLAUDE.md and /AGENTS.md back here and `git rm --cached` them.

